1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,312
Welcome to Unit Seven of Algebra One:
exponents and exponential functions.

2
00:00:05,762 --> 00:00:09,154
In this lesson, we'll learn the three main
exponent rules.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,165
An exponent counts repeated
multiplication. Two to the fourth means

4
00:00:15,165 --> 00:00:18,940
two times two times two times two, which
is sixteen.

5
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:22,270
The two is the base, and the four is the
exponent.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:28,307
Product rule: when you multiply powers
with the same base, add the exponents.

7
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:35,452
x squared times x cubed is x times x,
times x times x times x. That's x to the

8
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:35,967
fifth.

9
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:42,092
Quotient rule: when you divide powers with
the same base, subtract the exponents.

10
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:47,854
x to the seventh over x squared is x to
the fifth, because two of the x's cancel.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,373
Power rule: when you raise a power to a
power, multiply the exponents.

12
00:00:53,823 --> 00:00:58,559
x squared, all cubed, is x squared three
times, which is x to the sixth.

13
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:04,372
Now combine them. Simplify two x cubed,
times three x to the fourth.

14
00:01:04,822 --> 00:01:10,788
Multiply the numbers: two times three is
six. Add the exponents: x to the seventh.

15
00:01:10,788 --> 00:01:13,334
The answer is six x to the seventh.

16
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:19,693
Your turn. Simplify x to the fifth times x
cubed, all over x to the fourth.

17
00:01:20,143 --> 00:01:21,679
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:22,129 --> 00:01:27,294
The top is x to the eighth. Then eight
minus four is four. The answer is x to the

19
00:01:27,294 --> 00:01:27,740
fourth.

20
00:01:28,866 --> 00:01:34,019
What could two to the zero, or two to the
negative three, possibly mean? In this

21
00:01:34,019 --> 00:01:35,501
lesson, we'll find out.

22
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:41,308
Look at the pattern. Two cubed is eight,
two squared is four, two to the first is

23
00:01:41,308 --> 00:01:41,539
two.

24
00:01:41,989 --> 00:01:48,025
Each step down divides by two. So two to
the zero is one. In fact, any nonzero

25
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:50,501
number to the zero power is one.

26
00:01:51,633 --> 00:01:56,689
Keep going down the pattern. Two to the
negative one is one half, and two to the

27
00:01:56,689 --> 00:01:58,395
negative two is one fourth.

28
00:01:58,845 --> 00:02:04,586
A negative exponent means take the
reciprocal. x to the negative n equals one

29
00:02:04,586 --> 00:02:05,779
over x to the n.

30
00:02:06,899 --> 00:02:10,121
Five to the negative two is one over
twenty-five.

31
00:02:10,571 --> 00:02:16,333
And one over three to the negative two is
three squared, which is nine. A negative

32
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:18,933
exponent in the denominator moves up.

33
00:02:20,066 --> 00:02:23,650
Simplify x to the negative three times x
to the fifth.

34
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:28,623
Add the exponents: negative three plus
five is two. So it's x squared.

35
00:02:29,766 --> 00:02:34,523
A common mistake: a negative exponent does
not make the number negative.

36
00:02:34,973 --> 00:02:38,472
Two to the negative one is one half, not
negative two.

37
00:02:39,599 --> 00:02:44,165
Your turn. Simplify four to the negative
one, plus seven to the zero.

38
00:02:44,615 --> 00:02:46,151
Pause the video and try it.

39
00:02:46,601 --> 00:02:52,507
Four to the negative one is one fourth,
and seven to the zero is one. The total is

40
00:02:52,507 --> 00:02:53,875
one and one fourth.

41
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,276
Exponents don't have to be whole numbers.
In this lesson, we'll see what fractional

42
00:03:00,276 --> 00:03:01,229
exponents mean.

43
00:03:02,367 --> 00:03:07,753
Nine to the one half, squared, is nine to
the first, which is nine. So nine to the

44
00:03:07,753 --> 00:03:11,497
one half must be the square root of nine,
which is three.

45
00:03:11,947 --> 00:03:15,446
In general, x to the one half is the
square root of x.

46
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:21,508
The same idea works for cube roots. Eight
to the one third is the cube root of

47
00:03:21,508 --> 00:03:22,775
eight, which is two.

48
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:29,532
In general, x to the m over n is the n-th
root of x, raised to the m.

49
00:03:29,982 --> 00:03:33,566
The bottom of the fraction is the root,
and the top is the power.

50
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,556
Evaluate eight to the two thirds.

51
00:03:37,006 --> 00:03:41,664
The cube root of eight is two, and two
squared is four. So eight to the two

52
00:03:41,664 --> 00:03:42,595
thirds is four.

53
00:03:43,045 --> 00:03:45,605
Taking the root first keeps the numbers
small.

54
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:52,488
The exponent rules still apply. x to the
one half times x to the one half is x to

55
00:03:52,488 --> 00:03:54,051
the first, which is x.

56
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:58,336
Your turn. Evaluate twenty-seven to the
two thirds.

57
00:03:58,786 --> 00:04:00,322
Pause the video and try it.

58
00:04:00,772 --> 00:04:04,591
The cube root of twenty-seven is three,
and three squared is nine.

59
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:11,706
Scientists write huge and tiny numbers
with powers of ten. In this lesson, we'll

60
00:04:11,706 --> 00:04:13,648
learn scientific notation.

61
00:04:14,766 --> 00:04:19,054
A number in scientific notation looks like
a times ten to the n.

62
00:04:19,504 --> 00:04:23,963
The number a is at least one and less than
ten, and n is an integer.

63
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:28,812
Write three hundred forty thousand in
scientific notation.

64
00:04:29,262 --> 00:04:34,813
Move the decimal point five places to the
left to get three point four. So it's

65
00:04:34,813 --> 00:04:37,624
three point four times ten to the fifth.

66
00:04:38,766 --> 00:04:42,244
Now write zero point zero zero zero six
two.

67
00:04:42,694 --> 00:04:48,481
Move the decimal four places to the right
to get six point two. Small numbers get

68
00:04:48,481 --> 00:04:53,126
negative exponents: six point two times
ten to the negative four.

69
00:04:54,266 --> 00:04:57,850
To multiply, multiply the numbers and add
the exponents.

70
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:03,631
Three times ten to the fourth, times two
times ten to the fifth, is six times ten

71
00:05:03,631 --> 00:05:04,487
to the ninth.

72
00:05:05,633 --> 00:05:09,196
To divide, divide the numbers and subtract
the exponents.

73
00:05:09,646 --> 00:05:15,236
Eight times ten to the sixth, divided by
four times ten to the two, is two times

74
00:05:15,236 --> 00:05:16,494
ten to the fourth.

75
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:23,925
Your turn. Multiply five times ten cubed
by four times ten to the sixth. Remember,

76
00:05:23,925 --> 00:05:27,148
the answer must be in scientific notation.

77
00:05:27,598 --> 00:05:29,134
Pause the video and try it.

78
00:05:29,584 --> 00:05:35,667
Five times four is twenty, and three plus
six is nine. Twenty times ten to the ninth

79
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:37,840
is two times ten to the tenth.

80
00:05:38,966 --> 00:05:43,786
In this lesson, we'll meet exponential
functions, where the variable is in the

81
00:05:43,786 --> 00:05:44,342
exponent.

82
00:05:45,466 --> 00:05:50,671
An exponential function has the form f of
x equals a times b to the x.

83
00:05:51,121 --> 00:05:56,135
a is the starting value, and b is the
base, a positive number that isn't one.

84
00:05:57,266 --> 00:06:00,317
Make a table for f of x equals two to the
x.

85
00:06:00,767 --> 00:06:06,808
At x equals zero, the value is one. Then
two, four, eight. Each step multiplies by

86
00:06:06,808 --> 00:06:07,103
two.

87
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:13,449
Plot the points and connect them. The
curve rises slowly at first, then faster

88
00:06:13,449 --> 00:06:14,185
and faster.

89
00:06:14,635 --> 00:06:18,859
On the left, it gets close to zero but
never touches the x axis.

90
00:06:19,999 --> 00:06:26,314
Take f of x equals three times two to the
x. At x equals zero, f equals three.

91
00:06:26,764 --> 00:06:30,433
So a is the y intercept: the value where
the graph starts.

92
00:06:31,566 --> 00:06:34,019
Here's the key difference from linear
functions.

93
00:06:34,469 --> 00:06:39,582
A linear function adds the same amount
each step. An exponential function

94
00:06:39,582 --> 00:06:42,384
multiplies by the same factor each step.

95
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:49,705
Your turn. For f of x equals five times
three to the x, find f of zero and f of

96
00:06:49,705 --> 00:06:50,018
two.

97
00:06:50,468 --> 00:06:52,004
Pause the video and try it.

98
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:57,702
f of zero is five. f of two is five times
nine, which is forty-five.

99
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:04,190
Exponential functions model things that
grow or shrink by a percent. In this

100
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:06,940
lesson, we'll look at growth and decay.

101
00:07:08,066 --> 00:07:11,309
When the base b is greater than one, the
function grows.

102
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:17,257
A population of one hundred that doubles
each year is one hundred times two to the

103
00:07:17,257 --> 00:07:17,391
t.

104
00:07:18,533 --> 00:07:21,946
When b is between zero and one, the
function decays.

105
00:07:22,396 --> 00:07:27,687
A forty milligram dose that halves every
hour is forty times one half to the t.

106
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:32,524
For growth by a percent r, use b equals
one plus r.

107
00:07:32,974 --> 00:07:38,929
A two thousand dollar investment growing
five percent a year is two thousand times

108
00:07:38,929 --> 00:07:44,595
one point zero five to the t. After two
years, that's two thousand two hundred

109
00:07:44,595 --> 00:07:45,539
five dollars.

110
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:50,613
For decay by a percent r, use b equals one
minus r.

111
00:07:51,063 --> 00:07:56,021
A twenty thousand dollar car losing
fifteen percent each year is twenty

112
00:07:56,021 --> 00:07:59,234
thousand times zero point eight five to
the t.

113
00:08:00,366 --> 00:08:02,926
To decide growth or decay, look at the
base.

114
00:08:03,376 --> 00:08:09,463
One point zero three is greater than one:
growth of three percent. Zero point nine

115
00:08:09,463 --> 00:08:12,358
is less than one: decay of ten percent.

116
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:18,900
Your turn. A town of eight thousand grows
four percent per year. Write the model,

117
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,500
and find the population after one year.

118
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:23,486
Pause the video and try it.

119
00:08:23,936 --> 00:08:29,448
The model is eight thousand times one
point zero four to the t. After one year,

120
00:08:29,448 --> 00:08:32,448
that's eight thousand three hundred
twenty.

121
00:08:33,566 --> 00:08:39,446
In Unit Four we saw arithmetic sequences,
which add the same number each time. In

122
00:08:39,446 --> 00:08:45,107
this last lesson of Unit Seven, we'll see
geometric sequences, which multiply.

123
00:08:46,233 --> 00:08:50,670
In three, six, twelve, twenty-four, each
term is twice the one before.

124
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:56,432
The constant multiplier is called the
common ratio, r. Here r equals two.

125
00:08:57,566 --> 00:09:04,291
The formula for the n-th term is a sub n
equals a sub one times r to the n minus

126
00:09:04,291 --> 00:09:04,627
one.

127
00:09:05,077 --> 00:09:09,621
For our sequence, a sub n equals three
times two to the n minus one.

128
00:09:10,766 --> 00:09:12,174
Find the seventh term.

129
00:09:12,624 --> 00:09:17,674
Three times two to the sixth is three
times sixty-four, which is one hundred

130
00:09:17,674 --> 00:09:18,405
ninety-two.

131
00:09:19,533 --> 00:09:24,290
Compare. Two, five, eight, eleven adds
three each time, so it's arithmetic.

132
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:30,939
Two, six, eighteen, fifty-four multiplies
by three each time, so it's geometric. A

133
00:09:30,939 --> 00:09:36,004
geometric sequence is an exponential
function on the whole numbers.

134
00:09:37,133 --> 00:09:43,118
The ratio can be a fraction. In eighty,
forty, twenty, ten, the ratio is one half,

135
00:09:43,118 --> 00:09:44,578
so the terms shrink.

136
00:09:45,699 --> 00:09:50,478
Your turn. Find the sixth term of five,
fifteen, forty-five, and so on.

137
00:09:50,928 --> 00:09:52,464
Pause the video and try it.

138
00:09:52,914 --> 00:09:57,972
The ratio is three. Five times three to
the fifth is five times two hundred

139
00:09:57,972 --> 00:10:01,682
forty-three, which is one thousand two
hundred fifteen.

140
00:10:02,799 --> 00:10:07,540
That completes Unit Seven. Next, we'll
start Unit Eight: polynomials and

141
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:12,478
factoring. If this helped, subscribe to
School Math, Explained, and turn on

142
00:10:12,478 --> 00:10:15,770
notifications so you don't miss it. See
you there.

